WEBVTT

00:09.250 --> 00:10.130
What's wrong?

00:10.920 --> 00:13.290
Nothing. I'm fine.

00:13.920 --> 00:16.000
I'm here to listen if you need
to get something off your chest.

00:17.380 --> 00:18.380
All right.

00:19.540 --> 00:21.580
Then, hear me out...

00:29.380 --> 00:32.790
I'm in love with you.

00:46.540 --> 00:47.790
Why...?

00:52.210 --> 00:54.170
What is happening to me?

01:02.710 --> 01:04.500
Die, demon!

01:13.170 --> 01:16.380
The plan worked! Thanks for helping us kill this freak.

01:18.580 --> 01:19.790
C'mon. Let's go.

01:23.500 --> 01:26.750
I see. I've been betrayed.

01:27.540 --> 01:29.170
That she-devil is next!

01:29.170 --> 01:31.540
We should've done this a long time ago!

01:34.880 --> 01:39.540
So what if I'm bigger than most people?
How is that reason enough to kill me?

01:40.290 --> 01:41.500
Why is this happening?

01:42.630 --> 01:44.290
Why do I have to die?

01:49.080 --> 01:51.330
No.... not here...

01:54.290 --> 01:59.080
I don't want to die. Not here!

03:33.880 --> 03:34.880
Look!

03:34.880 --> 03:36.790
What's going on?!

03:42.920 --> 03:44.710
It shouldn't come as a surprise.

03:45.500 --> 03:47.830
This is what you wanted, isn't it?

04:13.710 --> 04:15.130
You're not going to run?

04:15.880 --> 04:19.040
I'm scared, but I won't run.

04:19.880 --> 04:23.460
Because even as a demon, I know that you're still you.

04:58.830 --> 04:59.880
I'm sorry...

05:01.380 --> 05:07.580
I couldn't stand strong like you did...

05:26.170 --> 05:27.330
I was wrong.

05:49.000 --> 05:50.630
What did I just see?

05:51.960 --> 05:53.170
Well, damn.

05:53.540 --> 05:58.540
Guess I can't absorb your power
when your mind is still intact.

06:00.330 --> 06:01.290
Suzune.

06:02.250 --> 06:05.130
So she's the reason why you fight, eh?

06:05.130 --> 06:08.880
Yes. I take it that you saw my memories as well?

06:09.920 --> 06:12.880
Seems like we're birds of a feather.

06:13.330 --> 06:14.290
Perhaps.

06:15.750 --> 06:17.460
You're not going to quit, are you?

06:18.170 --> 06:21.290
I wouldn't be a demon if I could exercise restraint.

06:22.080 --> 06:23.250
Good point.

06:23.960 --> 06:27.960
But no matter, you cannot overcome
my indomitable body.

06:28.330 --> 06:30.210
Indomitable, huh?

06:37.330 --> 06:40.250
This is pointless. Stop being stupid.

06:40.880 --> 06:45.460
I remember Mosuke. His only wish was to live
hidden from both demons and humans.

06:48.130 --> 06:53.290
And Hatsu. All she wanted was to return
to her husband as quickly as possible.

07:01.750 --> 07:06.080
And Ofuu. She only wished to go back
to her garden of happiness.

07:11.880 --> 07:16.170
And Yunagi. All she wanted was
to keep a single emotion secret.

07:18.330 --> 07:21.830
Long ago, there was a demon
who could see into the future.

07:22.210 --> 07:27.040
I imagine a need to change the doomed fate
of demonkind is what gave her that power.

07:27.460 --> 07:30.630
But in spite of her wishes, she could only see the future.

07:31.330 --> 07:34.330
It was an ability known as "foresight".

07:35.420 --> 07:37.290
It's all clear to me now.

07:37.630 --> 07:41.420
The powers we demons have are not skills, but desires.

07:41.790 --> 07:44.710
Negative emotions are what
transform humans into demons,

07:44.710 --> 07:47.750
but it's impossible wishes
that furnish demons with power.

07:48.380 --> 07:53.580
Or rather, their obsession is the paint
that covers their canvas of being.

07:54.380 --> 07:57.500
In which case, life will never go as they want.

07:59.170 --> 08:03.380
That's why I know.
Strength isn't what you wished for at all.

08:04.040 --> 08:07.750
Tsuchiura. What made you desire that indomitable body?

08:07.750 --> 08:08.670
Shut up!

08:09.040 --> 08:14.170
Allow me to change the question.
What is it you're fighting for?

08:17.960 --> 08:19.750
Trust me.

08:20.250 --> 08:24.710
Both demons and samurai are on the verge
of being abandoned by the modern age.

08:25.420 --> 08:29.960
We are relics of the past. That makes us compatriots.

08:30.250 --> 08:33.880
There is no good reason that we cannot join forces.

08:35.790 --> 08:40.040
Master Yasuhide generously
accepted me for the demon I am.

08:40.790 --> 08:43.210
My loyalty to him is everything.

08:43.790 --> 08:46.250
It's all that I have.

08:46.580 --> 08:48.750
No, there's more to your life than that.

08:49.670 --> 08:53.750
I figured you might be similar to me, but I was wrong.

08:54.500 --> 08:58.790
Tsuchiura. I'm fairly certain that you're stronger than I am.

08:59.420 --> 09:00.710
But I won't lose.

09:01.130 --> 09:06.250
You cast aside everything you had and
obtained strength by making yourself believe in a lie.

09:06.880 --> 09:11.920
Whereas my weakness has made me hesitant to cast
anything aside. So you'll never get the better of me!

09:12.750 --> 09:14.250
You're full of hot air.

09:14.580 --> 09:16.420
Act as tough as you want,

09:16.420 --> 09:19.000
you cannot bring any harm to me!

09:32.500 --> 09:33.500
Dart.

09:37.080 --> 09:40.500
Please forgive us. We're so sorry. Truly!

09:41.080 --> 09:43.210
Our daughter had no other choice!

09:43.210 --> 09:47.790
They threatened to ostracize our whole family
unless she helped them lure you into their trap!

09:47.790 --> 09:48.420
Shut up!

09:48.420 --> 09:51.580
She really did love you!

09:51.580 --> 09:53.500
I said shut up!

09:56.750 --> 10:01.960
Yeah. It didn't matter if you were a demon or not.
She believed in you wholeheartedly!

10:02.420 --> 10:04.080
No more!

10:04.960 --> 10:09.830
If I were indomitable, then I would
never have to fear being hurt again.

10:10.830 --> 10:15.750
If I were indomitable, then I would never
have to worry about facing death.

10:16.630 --> 10:18.710
If I were indomitable...

10:21.880 --> 10:25.210
then I could have fully believed in her.

10:35.920 --> 10:41.000
All I wanted... was someone to put my faith in...

10:57.170 --> 10:59.540
You're formidable.

11:00.540 --> 11:01.750
No, just weak.

11:02.380 --> 11:06.500
Tsuchiura. I think weakness is better for us in the end.

11:07.290 --> 11:11.500
We foolishly wanted to regain the things that we lost,
which drove us into becoming demons.

11:12.460 --> 11:18.500
Our half-hearted attempts to gain power and spurn
our weakness has trapped us on the wrong life path.

11:19.500 --> 11:21.500
But if our willpower had been a little weaker,

11:22.380 --> 11:25.330
then we could have simply died a respectable death.

11:26.170 --> 11:31.290
I see. We dug our graves in the wrong spot, huh?

11:31.750 --> 11:33.040
That sums it up.

11:33.500 --> 11:35.250
But this isn't so bad.

11:35.630 --> 11:39.380
I've recognized what my heart truly desired.

11:41.460 --> 11:43.880
Go on. Take my power.

11:44.500 --> 11:47.420
Although it was born from my pathetic obsession,

11:47.750 --> 11:50.000
it should prove handy at some point.

11:50.670 --> 11:53.080
I appreciate what you've done.

11:53.630 --> 11:58.580
Thank you for ending my life.
This isn't the worst place to die.

12:01.330 --> 12:07.630
I'm sorry, Master Yasuhide.
I was unable to grant your wish.

12:08.830 --> 12:14.420
It's strange. I can't bring myself to hate you,
even as you consume me.

12:14.880 --> 12:18.750
Perhaps, if we had met under different circumstances...

12:19.170 --> 12:23.630
Yeah. We could've been fighting
alongside each other instead.

12:26.130 --> 12:27.040
Exactly...

12:31.630 --> 12:32.540
Hey there!

12:33.130 --> 12:34.290
Welcome in!

12:34.580 --> 12:35.920
Took you long enough!

12:35.920 --> 12:37.830
Aw, gimme a break.

12:43.250 --> 12:45.290
Now then, shall we get going, Tsuchiura?

12:45.670 --> 12:46.540
Yeah.

12:49.670 --> 12:50.830
Safe travels!

12:52.880 --> 12:53.500
Thanks.

12:59.040 --> 13:00.040
Farewell.

13:14.540 --> 13:17.250
Ah, if it isn't Jinya-dono.

13:17.630 --> 13:19.580
Your being here can only mean one thing.

13:19.750 --> 13:23.920
Tsuchiura must be dead. Am I right?

13:24.500 --> 13:25.420
Yes.

13:25.920 --> 13:27.250
I see.

13:29.750 --> 13:33.580
Without Tsuchiura on my side,
I have no more moves to play.

13:33.880 --> 13:36.080
Checkmate, it would seem.

13:37.130 --> 13:38.290
That's right.

13:39.080 --> 13:41.880
And so, I've come to grant your wish.

13:42.920 --> 13:45.830
My wish, you say?

13:46.380 --> 13:49.830
Yes. I defeated Tsuchiura and consumed him.

13:50.290 --> 13:53.920
It's only fair that I take up the responsibility he left behind.

13:54.380 --> 13:58.000
Does that mean you will serve in his stead?

13:58.380 --> 13:59.170
No.

13:59.460 --> 14:02.500
I'm here to grant your heart's true desire.

14:04.830 --> 14:07.380
I always thought it was strange.

14:07.920 --> 14:13.330
Mataroku Sugino. Kiichi Okada.
And, of course, Tsuchiura.

14:13.960 --> 14:17.250
You've constantly made moves to provoke me.

14:19.630 --> 14:21.210
The question is: why?

14:21.710 --> 14:27.170
Your goal is supposedly to purge the foreigners
and reestablish the shogunate.

14:27.500 --> 14:29.420
But that isn't quite right.

14:31.040 --> 14:35.830
Because in reality you knew better than anyone
that foreign influence would never go away.

14:36.460 --> 14:40.420
Your true goal wasn't for success, but failure.

14:41.040 --> 14:45.380
For someone to step in and kill you.
That's what you want, right?

14:46.130 --> 14:48.750
I guess there's no point hiding it.

14:49.830 --> 14:51.540
I knew it all along.

14:52.130 --> 14:58.250
No matter how fiercely we resisted,
foreign culture would still find its way into this country.

14:58.710 --> 15:03.250
The government would collapse and
the age of samurai would come to an end.

15:03.830 --> 15:05.670
No one can stop that.

15:06.750 --> 15:09.210
I was fully aware.

15:09.960 --> 15:12.130
We must change with the times.

15:12.460 --> 15:17.960
All the people who choose to adapt
and welcome the new era are right to do so.

15:18.580 --> 15:21.420
However, it was simply beyond me.

15:22.130 --> 15:28.750
The thought of straying from the life path I've fought
so long and hard to forge seemed irrevocably shameful.

15:29.630 --> 15:32.380
And thus, I wanted to be killed.

15:32.960 --> 15:37.250
To die as a samurai who defended
the shogunate to the bitter end.

15:39.750 --> 15:44.420
So, it seems you really have
come to grant my true desire.

15:45.000 --> 15:46.920
We've both been a thorn in each other's side.

15:46.920 --> 15:48.880
Oh, most definitely.

15:49.210 --> 15:54.710
But that's just what happens when
we insist on having things go our way.

15:55.250 --> 15:56.170
You're not wrong.

16:00.880 --> 16:02.670
Will you kill me now?

16:03.580 --> 16:04.330
Yes.

16:09.000 --> 16:11.040
Though you failed to save the age of the samurai,

16:11.710 --> 16:14.080
you shall still meet a warrior's end.

16:21.750 --> 16:23.920
You are a demon enslaved to your blade.

16:25.130 --> 16:28.040
There is no place for you in the future.

16:28.960 --> 16:33.420
Both demons and katana are doomed
to be thrown out like yesterday's trash.

16:34.540 --> 16:38.000
So how will you continue to live in this world?

16:39.000 --> 16:47.380
Know that I'll be watching you...
with great interest... from beyond the grave...

17:06.540 --> 17:08.580
Daddy's taking a long time.

17:08.830 --> 17:10.380
He sure is.

17:13.460 --> 17:14.790
You're still awake?

17:15.500 --> 17:16.580
Daddy!

17:25.330 --> 17:27.750
Sorry. Didn't mean to keep you waiting.

17:28.210 --> 17:32.460
Jinya-kun. There's a better choice of words
for when you come home, you know?

17:34.960 --> 17:36.000
Daddy!

17:36.540 --> 17:39.000
Have you been a good girl, Nomari?

17:39.000 --> 17:39.750
Yeah!

17:42.880 --> 17:44.750
I think I need to leave Edo.

17:45.170 --> 17:48.500
It's only matter of time until word of
my being a demon spreads throughout town.

17:49.330 --> 17:50.670
I see.

17:51.880 --> 17:53.880
Well then, consider this.

17:54.420 --> 18:01.130
What if you followed my dad's advice
and took over as owner of the soba shop?

18:04.460 --> 18:05.670
Isn't that still a possibility?

18:05.960 --> 18:09.420
We can change the name. How about "Demon Soba"?

18:09.540 --> 18:11.790
A soba shop run by a married demon couple.

18:11.920 --> 18:13.580
Doesn't that sound amusing?

18:15.000 --> 18:17.500
I guess that would be kinda nice.

18:17.920 --> 18:20.000
Right? So, then...

18:22.290 --> 18:24.080
It's still a no, huh?

18:24.500 --> 18:26.830
I can't stray from my life path at this point.

18:27.750 --> 18:30.250
But you knew that already, didn't you?

18:32.750 --> 18:35.790
You really are the biggest hardhead alive.

18:36.330 --> 18:39.540
Yeah. Even I wish I didn't have to be like that.

18:40.330 --> 18:41.500
Listen, Ofuu.

18:42.330 --> 18:44.330
Although I might have made a huge mistake,

18:44.830 --> 18:47.000
I'm not depressed about it.

18:48.130 --> 18:51.540
I'm still unsure whether I'll be able
to forgive Suzune in the end or not.

18:52.210 --> 18:54.960
But there are people I can save even
if I stay on this flawed path.

18:55.290 --> 18:56.830
You helped me realize that.

18:57.460 --> 19:00.000
So I'm going to hem and haw for a little longer.

19:01.290 --> 19:02.580
Will you come with me?

19:09.880 --> 19:10.880
I'm sorry.

19:12.080 --> 19:13.830
I'm just hopeless, aren't I?

19:14.330 --> 19:16.380
Seeing you like that got me thinking...

19:16.830 --> 19:19.630
I took my dad's hand and let him lead me to the outside.

19:19.920 --> 19:23.250
Then I just lived under his wing the entire time.

19:24.000 --> 19:28.670
All I really did was stop relying on the comfort
of my memories to rely on him instead.

19:28.670 --> 19:31.170
So if I take your hand now,

19:31.630 --> 19:33.710
I know that I'll only end up dependent on you.

19:34.290 --> 19:38.830
Nothing will have changed from back when
I shut myself in the garden of happiness.

19:39.710 --> 19:41.920
That's too frustrating to live with, you know?

19:42.630 --> 19:47.580
So, although I'm the one who brought up
the idea of sticking together, I can't go with you.

19:47.580 --> 19:50.420
I have to learn how to make it on my own first.

19:51.080 --> 19:55.460
Otherwise, staying by your side
will only make me depressed.

19:56.460 --> 19:58.500
We're quite the awkward pair, eh?

19:58.880 --> 20:00.170
You can say that again.

20:01.790 --> 20:03.380
I need you to do me a favor.

20:03.710 --> 20:04.750
Could you please take Noma-

20:04.750 --> 20:07.250
No! I'm going with you, Daddy!

20:12.630 --> 20:13.960
You heard her.

20:14.880 --> 20:15.830
All right.

20:16.250 --> 20:17.380
Let's go together.

20:18.500 --> 20:19.460
Uh-huh!

20:25.710 --> 20:27.420
Will we see each other again?

20:27.880 --> 20:29.040
I don't know.

20:29.420 --> 20:31.580
But we won't be dying from old age any time soon.

20:31.580 --> 20:33.170
So we may bump into each other someday.

20:33.500 --> 20:37.330
Oh, come on. You know this is the part
you're supposed to just lie and say "yes".

20:37.880 --> 20:40.250
Too bad that demons never lie.

20:43.960 --> 20:45.750
So long, Ofuu.

20:46.380 --> 20:47.250
Bye.

20:48.000 --> 20:50.080
See you again. Someday.

21:06.540 --> 21:08.290
Are you happy, Daddy?

21:15.130 --> 21:18.040
Yeah. I suppose I must be.

21:19.250 --> 21:20.710
Hopefully we cross paths again.

21:24.630 --> 21:25.630
Goodbye.

21:26.920 --> 21:27.920
Ready to go?

21:27.920 --> 21:28.670
Yep!

21:31.830 --> 21:34.960
On October 14th, in the third year of the Keio era,

21:35.540 --> 21:39.920
the 15th Commander-in-Chief of the Edo shogunate,
Yoshinobu Tokugawa,

21:39.920 --> 21:42.420
ceded his political authority to the Emperor.

21:43.130 --> 21:46.040
This event was widely known as the "Return of Power".

21:47.290 --> 21:50.630
And thus, the long-running age
of the samurai came to an end,

21:50.630 --> 21:54.040
and a brand new era was ushered in.

22:29.830 --> 22:31.670
Are you happy, Daddy?

22:32.210 --> 22:35.000
Yeah. I suppose I must be.

22:36.880 --> 22:38.420
Hopefully we cross paths again.

22:41.960 --> 22:43.130
What's the matter?

22:44.130 --> 22:46.290
I saw someone who brought back memories.

22:46.670 --> 22:48.250
Who might that be?

22:49.750 --> 22:52.380
A person whose feelings I once hurt.

22:53.880 --> 22:56.830
I'm sorry. I shouldn't be holding us up!

22:57.210 --> 22:59.130
Let's go, darling.

22:59.130 --> 23:01.880
Okay, I suppose it's about time
we head back to the shop...

23:02.210 --> 23:03.920
Lady Natsu.

23:04.330 --> 23:05.330
Darling!

23:06.130 --> 23:10.170
Shucks, don't mind me. I just had a feeling...

23:10.170 --> 23:13.250
it'd be good to call you that for old time's sake.

23:13.670 --> 23:14.710
I wonder why?

23:16.170 --> 23:18.170
Well, get your butt in gear...

23:18.170 --> 23:19.250
Zenji!

23:19.250 --> 23:21.000
Right away, milady!

23:22.830 --> 23:25.460
Man, it's been way too long. This is making me blush!

23:25.580 --> 23:27.540
And how do you think I feel?!

23:32.710 --> 23:34.960
Farewell, Jinya.
